# Paths the `tauri dev` file watcher must not treat as source changes.
#
# This file exists because the watcher reads only `.taurignore` and
# `src-tauri/.gitignore`. Every path below is *already* ignored by the repo-root
# `.gitignore`, but that file is invisible to the watcher, so it saw generated and
# staged output as real edits, killed the running app, and restarted the whole Rust
# build — repeatedly, and mid-flight. On Windows that also risks relinking
# `pragma.exe` while the previous dev instance still holds a lock on it.
#
# Uses .gitignore syntax. Patterns are intentionally unanchored so they also apply
# inside the Cargo path dependencies the watcher follows (`packages/constants`,
# `crates/*`), not just under `src-tauri/`.

# Generated TypeScript from packages/constants. `tauri:dev` regenerates this via
# `predev` -> `@pragma/constants generate` on every start. Rust never reads it: the
# Rust types come from `typify::import_types!("schema.json")` at compile time, so
# schema.json itself stays watched and still triggers a rebuild when it changes.
**/src/generated/

# Sidecar binaries and bundled plugin resources, staged by
# scripts/stage-daemon-sidecar.sh immediately before `tauri dev` starts.
binaries/
resources/plugins/
